<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bamako</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bamako is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger River</a> in the south-west of the country. A small trading town when French troops built a fort there in 1883, it became the capital of the colony of Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> and Niger in 1908 and later of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, linked to the coast by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dakar-niger-railway">Dakar–Niger Railway</a>. It has been Mali's capital since independence in 1960.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bamako.jpg" alt="Bamako" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rgaudin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Place_de_la_libert%C3%A9_-_Bamako.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
